## Credential references (names only, never values)
- IC read-only token: `op://Automation/Investing Companion - Secrets/IC_API_TOKEN`
  Resolve it into the environment only for the command that needs it: put
  `IC_API_TOKEN="op://Automation/Investing Companion - Secrets/IC_API_TOKEN"` in a gitignored
  env-file such as `.env.local`, then run
  `OP_CONNECT_HOST=http://<connect-host>:8090 ~/.claude/scripts/op-resolve.py --env-file .env.local -- hub ic pull`.
  The hub reads only `IC_API_TOKEN`; it never calls the credential manager itself.
- Market data key (Massive): `op://Automation/Investing Companion - Secrets/MASSIVE_API_KEY`
  Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` (gitignored) and start Claude Code with `scripts/hub-session.sh`
  so the key reaches the `massive` MCP server as `MASSIVE_API_KEY` and the IC token reaches the
  SessionStart hook. The launcher picks one of three paths (README § Massive): `connect` (export
  `OP_CONNECT_HOST=http://<connect-host>:8090`), `op` (signed-in 1Password CLI), or `env` (export
  `MASSIVE_API_KEY` and `IC_API_TOKEN` yourself; no `.env.local` needed). Force one with
  `HUB_SESSION_MODE=connect|op|env`. The resolvers never print secrets.
  Equivalent for Connect: `OP_CONNECT_HOST=http://<connect-host>:8090 ~/.claude/scripts/op-resolve.py --env-file .env.local -- claude`
  One-time setup: `uv tool install --with 'mcp<2' "mcp_massive @ git+https://github.com/massive-com/mcp_massive@v0.10.0"`
  and `cp .mcp.json.example .mcp.json`

